  "ts": "2026-05-26T08:31:50.914316Z",
  "content": "Currency is stored as int64 microcents (10⁻⁶ cent = 10⁻⁸ dollar) in column cost_microcents_usd - NOT whole cents and NOT floats. Tom originally asked for whole cents but I pushed back: per-call costs are routinely sub-cent (claude-haiku ~0.3 cents, embedding ~0.0002 cents), so whole-cent rounding would zero out almost every call. Conversion: divide by 10⁶ for cents, 10⁸ for dollars. computeCost in internal/ai/pricing.go does float math internally then rounds at the int64 boundary so aggregation stays exact.",
  "tags": [
    "storage",
    "currency",
    "gotcha"
  ],
